--- !u!114 &573886142
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 573886131}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 064fac1e0032bdb4eb7c9ba5a030f152, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ButtonLocalizedTextController
  targetText: {fileID: 754325187}
  backgroundRect: {fileID: 1195132667}
  backgroundVerticalPadding: 1.5
  minimumTextHeight: 0.5
  growDownwardOnly: 1
  keepBackgroundCurrentTop: 1
  targetCamera: {fileID: 2137303996}
  items:
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 311395521}
      line: {fileID: 88718941}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1967128947}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: 'Aortic Arch:

      -------------

      -is the curved portion of the
      aorta that connects the ascending and descending aorta, distributing oxygen-rich
      blood to the head, neck, and upper limbs.

      -beginning at the level of
      the second sternocostal joint and extending to the fourth thoracic vertebra
      (T4).

      -It curves posteriorly and to the left.

      -gives rise to
      three major arteries: Brachiocephalic trunk, Left common carotid artery & Left
      subclavian artery.

'
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 871718269}
      line: {fileID: 1895774755}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1510511170}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Superior Vena Cava: (SVC) \n------------------------------\n-is a large,
      valveless vein that returns deoxygenated blood from the upper half of the body
      to the right atrium of the heart.\n-centimeters long and 2 centimeters in diameter.\n-located
      in the anterior right superior mediastinum.\n-It is formed by the union of
      the left and right brachiocephalic veins.\n-terminates in the upper part of
      the right atrium.\n"
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 653012696}
      line: {fileID: 1465346096}
      targetModel: {fileID: 230049641}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: 'Pulmonary Artery:

      -------------------

      -is a blood vessel
      that carries deoxygenated blood from the right side of the heart to the lungs
      for oxygenation.

      -Originate from right ventricle of the heart & branches
      into right and left pulmonary arteries.

'
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 615688123}
      line: {fileID: 2127033128}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1333668818}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: 'Left Atrial Auricle

      -------------------

      -also known as the
      left atrial appendage (LAA).

      -flap or thin pouch of the heart wall located
      on the anterior surface of the left atrium.

      -It is remanent of fetal
      left heart.

'
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 1905892178}
      line: {fileID: 476330892}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1333668818}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Right Atrium\n--------------\r\n- is the heart\u2019s upper-right chamber
      that receives deoxygenated blood from the body and directs it to the right
      ventricle through the tricuspid valve.\r\n- forms the right border of the heart
      in the mediastinum.\r\n- thin-walled, low-pressure chamber.\r\n- receives blood
      from the superior vena cava (SVC), inferior vena cava (IVC), and coronary sinus.\r\n"
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 67528618}
      line: {fileID: 162255114}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1413219524}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Left Ventricle\n---------------\r\n- is the heart\u2019s lower left chamber
      responsible for pumping oxygenated blood to the entire body.\r\n- forming the
      heart\u2019s apex.\r\n- contributing to the anterior, diaphragmatic, and apex
      surfaces of the heart.\r\n- has the thickest myocardium of all heart chambers.\r\n-
      Two key valves regulate blood flow in and out of the left ventricle: Mitral
      (bicuspid) valve: Located between the left atrium and left ventricle & Aortic
      valve: Situated at the opening to the aorta.\r\n"
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 1610853090}
      line: {fileID: 855499153}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1789041975}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Right Ventricle\n-----------------\r\n- is the heart chamber responsible
      for pumping deoxygenated blood to the lungs for oxygenation through the pulmonary
      valve into the pulmonary artery, directing it to the lungs for oxygenation.\r\n-
      with walls thinner than the left ventricle (about 3\u20135 mm) because it pumps
      blood a shorter distance at lower pressure."
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 974258130}
      line: {fileID: 1471193996}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1413219524}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Coronary Sulcus\n-------------------\r\n- Also known as the atrioventricular
      groove.\r\n- Is a shallow groove on the heart\u2019s surface that separates
      the atria from the ventricles and contains major coronary vessels.\r\n"
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 1426513829}
      line: {fileID: 1822811935}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1333668818}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Pulmonary Veins\n------------------\r\n- are blood vessels that carry
      oxygen-rich blood from the lungs to the left atrium of the heart. \r\n- The
      only veins in the body that carry oxygen-rich blood.\r\n- are part of the pulmonary
      circulation.\r\n- Most people have four pulmonary veins, two from each lung
      (superior & inferior)\r\n- These veins originate in the lungs at the hilum
      pass through the posterior mediastinum and empty into the left atrium of the
      heart.\r\n"
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 1345778727}
      line: {fileID: 1376999245}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1375347430}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Pulmonary Valve\n------------------\r\n- is a semilunar heart valve that
      controls blood flow from the right ventricle to the pulmonary artery, ensuring
      blood moves toward the lungs without backflow.\r\n- consists of three crescent-shaped
      cusps or leaflets\u2014commonly named right, left, and anterior.\r\n"
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 946194540}
      line: {fileID: 1599422777}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1337046905}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: "Tricuspid Valve\n----------------\r\n- s a one-way heart valve that controls
      blood flow from the right atrium to the right ventricle and prevents backflow.\r\n-
      has three leaflets or cusps\u2014anterior, posterior, and septal\u2014that
      open and close with each heartbeat.\r\n- These leaflets are anchored by chordae
      tendineae to the papillary muscles of the right ventricle, which prevent the
      valve from inverting during ventricular contraction."
  - buttons:
    - button: {fileID: 1606066605}
      line: {fileID: 2100672332}
      targetModel: {fileID: 1804506078}
      followScale: 1
      buttonAlwaysFacesCamera: 1
      buttonCameraRotationOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      lineLocalRotation: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
      lineScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonLocalPosition: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      buttonScaleRatio: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
      initializedTarget: {fileID: 0}
      initializedLine: {fileID: 0}
      initializedButton: {fileID: 0}
      initialized: 0
    text: 'Mitral Valve

      -------------

      - s a heart valve located between
      the left atrium and left ventricle that ensures one-way blood flow from the
      atrium to the ventricle.

      - It is a bicuspid valve as it has two leaflets
      (cusps): an anterior and a posterior leaflet.

'
